\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let $k$ be algebraically closed, let $X/k$ be a smooth projective geometrically connected curve, and let $G$ be reductive, with $\operatorname{char}(k)$ greater than the Coxeter number of $G$. In the corresponding derived $\ell$-adic setting, prove the canonical equivalence $\operatorname{Shv}_{\operatorname{Nilp}}(\operatorname{Bun}_G)\simeq\operatorname{IndCoh}_{\operatorname{Nilp}}(\operatorname{LocSys}^{\operatorname{restr}}_{\widehat G})$.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2021/39}{[S2]}.

